poll() of Cosmopolitan on Windows (libc/calls/poll-nt.c, C61 and C62 of
docs/UPSTREAM.md):

- The libc took its fast path, one WSAPoll() and one
  WaitForMultipleObjects(), only for 63 fds or fewer. WSAPoll() takes any
  count of sockets; only the files and pipes of WaitForMultipleObjects()
  have a limit of 63. Now the fast path takes any count of sockets, in
  arrays on the heap for more than 64 sockets.
- With more than 63 files and pipes, the other path polls parts of the
  set and then waits with _park_norestart(). That function takes a time
  of the wall clock, and the libc gave it a time of the monotonic clock,
  a date in 1970: the wait ended at once, and the loop used a whole CPU.
  Now it gets the time of the wall clock, as in clock_nanosleep-nt.c.
  The parts have 63 fds, so that each part has 63 files or fewer.

scripts/steps.sh builds the file with this patch for the x86_64 half
(build_cosmo_file), and applies it to the libc of Windows on ARM64
(build_cosmo_libc).

--- a/libc/calls/poll-nt.c
+++ b/libc/calls/poll-nt.c
